CORE
runtime.c
--pointer-check
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main\.precondition_instance\.1\] line 16 static array parameter x must provide access to its declared minimum: FAILURE$
^\[main\.precondition_instance\.2\] line 17 static array parameter x must provide access to its declared minimum: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.precondition_instance\.3\] line 18 static array parameter x must provide access to its declared minimum: FAILURE$
^\[main\.no-body\.two_declarations\] line 16 no body for callee two_declarations: FAILURE$
^\*\* 3 of \d+ failed
--
^warning: ignoring
INVARIANT
--
A later prototype-only declaration strengthens a constant minimum. Runtime
minima from declarations with different parameter names are renamed to the
definition's parameters and combined into their maximum, so 3 + 2 elements are
required.
